# Line endings.
#
# These scripts are written on Windows and executed on the board: they are copied
# over with scp, not through git, so `core.autocrlf` cannot fix them on the way.
# A CRLF shell script dies on Linux at the first line — the shebang or the next
# line comes back as `$'\r': command not found` — which is how probe-onnx.sh
# failed on K1 (2026-09-10) after a plain scp from a Windows checkout.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree, not just the index. The index was already LF;
# only the checkout was converted, and the checkout is what gets copied.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.rs    text eol=lf

# Never line-ending convert anything binary. `duck-detect/models/` holds the
# NPU runtime's own inputs; a stray CR would corrupt them silently.
*.onnx  binary
*.rknn  binary
*.so     binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.pdf   binary
